          1.075,
          1.052
        ],
        "median_ms": 1.075,
        "note": "Agrees with the sweep's 1.081 ms plain record for the same tile, so the two runs are comparable to within about 0.5 percent."
      },
      {
        "tile": [
          32,
          64,
          32
        ],
        "samples_ms": [
          1.11,
          1.055,
          1.063
        ],
        "median_ms": 1.063
      }
    ],
    "decomposition_ms": {
      "committed_tile_plain": 1.081,
      "plain_at_32_32_32": 1.025,
      "blocked_at_32_32_32": 0.948,
      "tile_shape_effect": 0.056,
      "staging_effect_at_same_tile": 0.077
    },
    "conclusion": "About 42 percent of the apparent 0.948-versus-1.081 gap is the tile shape and only the remaining 0.077 ms is attributable to the blocked staging, roughly 7 percent at that tile. The two numbers still come from separate runs rather than one interleaved pass, so the split is indicative, not exact. It does not change the outcome: the kernel is incorrect at every tile, all six ffn_down variants fail outright, and the 0.948 ms is not credited as performance anywhere.",
    "caveat": "This probe measures plain staging only. Re-measuring the blocked variant interleaved with it would require restoring the reverted rhs_block pass-through, which was not done because the variant fails the correctness gate and cannot be shipped."
  },
